<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Question and computational graph for a GSM8K problem (final answer: <span id="A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">48</span>).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We generated the computational graphs for all of the problems in GSM8k and AIME24 datasets to examine the patterns of computation and compositions for these problems. While the graphs for these two datasets are not equivalent as they use different operators, they give some insights into why our method is able to show generalization across different datasets. For GSM8k problems, we found the computational graphs have average width and height of 4.1 and 4.0 respectively, while AIME graphs have average width and height of 6.6 and 7.1 respectively. We then compare the statistics for the graphs of AIME problems solved before and after our procedure as shown in Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix A Compositions and Computational Graphs. ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. We observe that our method enables models to solve significantly deeper computational graphs, which we speculate generalizes to harder problems such as AIME.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>AIME24 solved problems comparison. <span id="A1.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">N+E</span> denotes Nodes + Edges.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T3.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T3.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">N+E</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Width</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Height</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Baseline: Instruct-model solved problems</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">47.25</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">8</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">6.75</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.4.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T3.4.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Ours: Additional newly solved problems</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">54.3</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">4.7</td>
<td id="A1.T3.4.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">10.3</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Setup and notation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the simplified model of long-horizon skills from Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Method ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> to analyse curriculum benefits for LHR. Consider a finite-horizon episodic problem with maximum horizon <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. At each step <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,\dots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,\dots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math> there is a binary correctness indicator <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math> iff step <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is correct. Write <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{&lt;j}:=\prod_{\ell&lt;j}C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{&lt;j}:=\prod_{\ell&lt;j}C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\leq j}:=\prod_{\ell\leq j}C_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\leq j}:=\prod_{\ell\leq j}C_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>. The policy <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> (language model) generates a response <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=(y_{1},\dots,y_{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(y_{1},\dots,y_{H})</annotation></semantics></math> autoregressively by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{k}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,y_{\leq k}),\qquad k=1,\dots,H," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{k}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x,y_{\leq k}),\qquad k=1,\dots,H,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and we suppress explicit dependence on <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> below. A verifier <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}(y)\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}(y)\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> pays <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> iff <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\leq i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\leq i}</annotation></semantics></math> is correct, i.e. <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{i}(y)=\mathbb{I}\{C_{\leq i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}(y)=\mathbb{I}\{C_{\leq i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Method ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\theta_{0})\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\theta_{0})\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denote <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">atomic task reliability</em> and let <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}(\theta_{j})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}(\theta_{j})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> denote <em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">context-length–dependent reliability</em> with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume disjoint depth parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and a shared atomic block <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting that training strictly below depth <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> cannot improve the skill captured by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}:=p(\theta_{0})\,\sigma_{j}(\theta_{j})\;=\;\mathbb{P}(C_{j}=1\mid C_{&lt;j}=1),\qquad q_{j}\in(0,1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}:=p(\theta_{0})\,\sigma_{j}(\theta_{j})\;=\;\mathbb{P}(C_{j}=1\mid C_{&lt;j}=1),\qquad q_{j}\in(0,1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\;:=\;\prod_{j=1}^{i}q_{j}\;=\;\mathbb{P}(C_{\leq i}=1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\;:=\;\prod_{j=1}^{i}q_{j}\;=\;\mathbb{P}(C_{\leq i}=1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We assume that at initialization <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For a chosen training horizon <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}}[R_{h}(y)]\;=\;s_{h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{\theta}}[R_{h}(y)]\;=\;s_{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and for <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=H</annotation></semantics></math> we write <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)=J_{H}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)=J_{H}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We use REINFORCE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams, 1992</a>)</cite> with an unbiased advantage estimator with <em id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">constant</em> baseline equal to the same-horizon mean <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}=s_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}=s_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> (the form approximated by GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>). For a parameter block <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}\big[(R_{h}-\mu_{h})\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\big],\qquad\bar{g}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(R_{h}(y_{i})-\mu_{h})\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\;=\;\mathbb{E}\big[(R_{h}-\mu_{h})\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\big],\qquad\bar{g}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(R_{h}(y_{i})-\mu_{h})\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant, <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Per-update improvement and batch size</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite> in analysing the expected improvement of our policy when taking updates <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{+}_{k}=\theta_{k}+\eta\bar{g}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{+}_{k}=\theta_{k}+\eta\bar{g}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under the assumption that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth in <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, taking this update (holding all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed) results in expected improvement (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Duchi, 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck, 2015</a></cite>)</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\Big(1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\tfrac{1}{\mathrm{SNR}(\theta_{k})}\right)\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>SNR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\Big(1-\tfrac{L\eta}{2}\left(1+\tfrac{1}{\mathrm{SNR}(\theta_{k})}\right)\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;:=\;\frac{\|\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}}{\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;:=\;\frac{\|\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}}{\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Without loss of generality, view <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> only. Given <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, applying the descent lemma to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-J_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-J_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> gives, for any <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{h}(\theta_{k}+u)\;\geq\;J_{h}(\theta_{k})+\langle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta),u\rangle-\tfrac{L}{2}\|u\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{h}(\theta_{k}+u)\;\geq\;J_{h}(\theta_{k})+\langle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta),u\rangle-\tfrac{L}{2}\|u\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\eta\bar{g}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\eta\bar{g}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and taking expectation over the randomness in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\big\langle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta),\,\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\big\rangle\;-\;\tfrac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\big\langle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta),\,\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\big\rangle\;-\;\tfrac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Decomposing <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}\;+\;\|\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}=\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}\;+\;\|\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and recalling that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\;-\;\tfrac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\Big(\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}+\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\eta\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\;-\;\tfrac{L\eta^{2}}{2}\Big(\mathbb{E}\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\|^{2}+\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">and simple rearrangement results in the form in equation <a href="#A2.E3" title="In B.2 Per-update improvement and batch size ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
 <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Optimising over <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\underbrace{\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}}{2L}}_{:=\,\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}}\cdot\frac{1}{1+1/\mathrm{SNR}(\theta_{k})}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.448em">=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>SNR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[J_{h}(\theta^{+})-J_{h}(\theta)\right]\;\geq\;\underbrace{\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{h}(\theta)\|^{2}}{2L}}_{:=\,\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}}\cdot\frac{1}{1+1/\mathrm{SNR}(\theta_{k})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">To achieve a fraction <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> of the noiseless gain <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}</annotation></semantics></math> it suffices that</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{1-\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;\geq\;\frac{\beta}{1-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the quantities <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(0)}_{k,h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> determine how much we can improve our policy by, and how many samples <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> will be required to do so.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Signal-to-noise ratio</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a training horizon <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>. Abbreviate</p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s:=s_{k-1},\qquad q:=q_{k},\qquad T:=\prod_{j=k+1}^{h}q_{j}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:=s_{k-1},\qquad q:=q_{k},\qquad T:=\prod_{j=k+1}^{h}q_{j},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}=s\,q\,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}=s\,q\,T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=k</annotation></semantics></math>. Because <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> only affects <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]\;=\;\nabla_{\theta_{k}}s_{h}\;=\;s\,T\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\bar{g}_{k}]\;=\;\nabla_{\theta_{k}}s_{h}\;=\;s\,T\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For the variance, note that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(C_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}{=}1)=\Big(\frac{C_{k}}{q}-\frac{1-C_{k}}{1-q}\Big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}=\frac{C_{k}-q}{q(1-q)}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(C_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}{=}1)=\Big(\frac{C_{k}}{q}-\frac{1-C_{k}}{1-q}\Big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}=\frac{C_{k}-q}{q(1-q)}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> vanishes unless <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{&lt;k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{&lt;k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. A direct enumeration over <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(C_{&lt;k},C_{k},C_{k+1:h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C_{&lt;k},C_{k},C_{k+1:h})</annotation></semantics></math> with the constant baseline <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}=s\,q\,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}=s\,q\,T</annotation></semantics></math> gives the conditional second moment</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[(R_{h}-\mu_{h})^{2}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,C_{&lt;k}=1\right]=\;T\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-2(1-q))}{q(1-q)}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[(R_{h}-\mu_{h})^{2}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,C_{&lt;k}=1\right]=\;T\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-2(1-q))}{q(1-q)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We therefore obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|\bar{g}_{k}-\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}\big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\frac{s}{N}\;T\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-3(1-q))}{q(1-q)}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\frac{s}{N}\;T\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-3(1-q))}{q(1-q)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">The exact SNR is then</p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,T\,q(1-q)}{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-3(1-q))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,T\,q(1-q)}{(1-q)+s\,q\,T\,(s\,q-3(1-q))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">In the long-horizon regime <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the denominator is <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-q)\,(1+O(T))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-q)\,(1+O(T))</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;=\;N\,s\,q\,T\left(1+O\!\left(\tfrac{T}{1-q}\right)\right)\;=\;\Theta(N\,s\,q\,T)\;=\;\Theta(N\,s_{h})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{h}(\theta_{k})\;=\;N\,s\,q\,T\left(1+O\!\left(\tfrac{T}{1-q}\right)\right)\;=\;\Theta(N\,s\,q\,T)\;=\;\Theta(N\,s_{h}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Regimes and consequences</h3>

<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Single-step only (train only at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When training only at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the required batch size and per-update noiseless improvement clearly do not depend on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Training at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> changes <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\theta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\theta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> but cannot change <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, so even <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the long-horizon ceiling at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j=2}^{H}\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j=2}^{H}\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Nevertheless, for any target success probability <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, improving <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> increases the largest <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h}\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h}\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\;=\;\frac{\ln c-\sum_{j=2}^{h}\ln\sigma_{j}}{\ln p}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\;=\;\frac{\ln c-\sum_{j=2}^{h}\ln\sigma_{j}}{\ln p}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Direct full horizon (train only at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=H</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> at initialisation, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{H}=\Theta(\alpha^{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{H}=\Theta(\alpha^{H})</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and by equation <a href="#A2.E9" title="In B.3 Signal-to-noise ratio ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{H}(\theta_{k})\;=\;\Theta(N\,s_{H})\;=\;\Theta(N\,\alpha^{H})\qquad(k\geq 1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{H}(\theta_{k})\;=\;\Theta(N\,s_{H})\;=\;\Theta(N\,\alpha^{H})\qquad(k\geq 1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">To keep a constant fraction of the noiseless gain one must therefore take</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta(\alpha^{-H})\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta(\alpha^{-H})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">while the noiseless improvement for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,H}\;=\;\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{H}\|^{2}}{2L}\;=\;\frac{(s_{k-1}T_{k+1:H})^{2}}{2L}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\;=\;\Theta\!\big(\alpha^{2H}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,H}\;=\;\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{H}\|^{2}}{2L}\;=\;\frac{(s_{k-1}T_{k+1:H})^{2}}{2L}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\;=\;\Theta\!\big(\alpha^{2H}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The required batch size to achieve a constant fraction of the noiseless improvement is exponential, while the noiseless improvement decays exponentially, making training directly at large <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> effectively impossible. In fact, direct training at horizon <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is worse than single-step training, as the signal is too small to effectively raise <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mathrm{SNR}_{H}(\theta_{0})=\Theta(N\,H\,\alpha^{H})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>H</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mathrm{SNR}_{H}(\theta_{0})=\Theta(N\,H\,\alpha^{H})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Curriculum over depths (train at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=k</annotation></semantics></math> and advance when <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a target success probability <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{H}\geq c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{H}\geq c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can ensure that curriculum training achieves this by only progressing the horizon <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)^{H}\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>H</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)^{H}\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim(-\ln c)/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim(-\ln c)/H</annotation></semantics></math>. If we assume that the earlier stages have been learned so <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k-1}\geq(1-\varepsilon)^{k-1}\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k-1}\geq(1-\varepsilon)^{k-1}\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>, then from equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="In B.3 Signal-to-noise ratio ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> we have that,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SNR}_{k}(\theta_{k})=\Theta\!\left(N\,\frac{q_{k}(1-q_{k})}{(2q_{k}-1)^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SNR}_{k}(\theta_{k})=\Theta\!\left(N\,\frac{q_{k}(1-q_{k})}{(2q_{k}-1)^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The SNR is minimised near the target <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}=1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}=1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{q_{k}(1-q_{k})}{(2q_{k}-1)^{2}}\asymp\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≍</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{q_{k}(1-q_{k})}{(2q_{k}-1)^{2}}\asymp\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. To realise a fixed fraction of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(0)}_{k,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(0)}_{k,k}</annotation></semantics></math> it suffices, by equation <a href="#A2.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Per-update improvement and batch size ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, to take</p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right)\;=\;\Theta(H)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right)\;=\;\Theta(H).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">At <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{k}=s_{k-1}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{k}=s_{k-1}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the noiseless gain is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,k}\;=\;\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{k}\|^{2}}{2L}\;=\;\frac{s_{k-1}^{2}}{2L}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,k}\;=\;\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}J_{k}\|^{2}}{2L}\;=\;\frac{s_{k-1}^{2}}{2L}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">independent of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>. Provided <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> does not decay faster than polynomially as <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\to 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\to 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, curriculum yields polynomial sample complexity in <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uniform mixture over lengths.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sample <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1{:}H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Unif</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\sim\mathrm{Unif}\{1{:}H\}</annotation></semantics></math> and run the depth-<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> estimator; for parameters <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the per<em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">-iteration</em> SNR obtained for its update averages to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{I}[\mathrm{SNR}_{I}(\theta_{i})]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{i-1}\,q_{i}\;\sum_{t=0}^{H-i}T_{i+1:i+t}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{I}[\mathrm{SNR}_{I}(\theta_{i})]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{i-1}\,q_{i}\;\sum_{t=0}^{H-i}T_{i+1:i+t}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Frontier phase.</em> We say horizon <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is at the frontier when earlier skills are sufficiently reliable while deeper ones are not yet learnt, namely</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{i-1}\geq c\quad\text{for some fixed }c\in(0,1)\qquad\text{and}\qquad\sum_{t=0}^{H-i}T_{i+1:i+t}=\Theta(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi><mtext>for some fixed </mtext><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>and</mtext><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i-1}\geq c\quad\text{for some fixed }c\in(0,1)\qquad\text{and}\qquad\sum_{t=0}^{H-i}T_{i+1:i+t}=\Theta(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During this frontier phase,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{I}[\mathrm{SNR}_{I}(\theta_{i})]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{i-1}\,q_{i}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{I}[\mathrm{SNR}_{I}(\theta_{i})]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{i-1}\,q_{i}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Whenever we sample a batch with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=i</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the same noiseless improvement and batch size scaling as curriculum training, with</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\epsilon}\right)=\Theta(H),\qquad\Delta^{(0)}_{i,i}=\Theta\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{i}}q_{i}\|^{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N=\Theta\left(\frac{1}{\epsilon}\right)=\Theta(H),\qquad\Delta^{(0)}_{i,i}=\Theta\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{i}}q_{i}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Whenever we sample <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>, we see negligible change as samples with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&lt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&lt;i</annotation></semantics></math> cannot improve <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and samples with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;i</annotation></semantics></math> have per-iteration gain that scales with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{h-1}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{h-1}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{I}[\Delta_{h}\ \text{per iter}]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{h-1}^{3}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{i}}q_{h}\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>per iter</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{I}[\Delta_{h}\ \text{per iter}]\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{N}{H}\;s_{h-1}^{3}\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{i}}q_{h}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, it takes <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim H</annotation></semantics></math> times longer to train with uniform sampling than with curriculum, due to only a fraction <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/H</annotation></semantics></math> of the updates being “useful” at each frontier <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\cdots,H\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\cdots,H\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Dense rewards</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now analyse the reward-to-go estimator <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Williams, 1992</a>; <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sutton et al., 1999</a>)</cite> with <em id="A2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dense rewards</em>. For a fixed training horizon <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq k</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{t}(y)\;:=\;\mathbb{I}\{C_{\leq t}=1\},\qquad G_{k}(y)\;:=\;\sum_{t=k}^{h}R_{t}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{t}(y)\;:=\;\mathbb{I}\{C_{\leq t}=1\},\qquad G_{k}(y)\;:=\;\sum_{t=k}^{h}R_{t}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the return-to-go from step <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. As before, write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s:=s_{k-1}=\prod_{j&lt;k}q_{j},\qquad q:=q_{k},\qquad T_{k+1:k+t}:=\prod_{j=k+1}^{k+t}q_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>T</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s:=s_{k-1}=\prod_{j&lt;k}q_{j},\qquad q:=q_{k},\qquad T_{k+1:k+t}:=\prod_{j=k+1}^{k+t}q_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">On <em id="A2.SS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reach</em> (<math id="A2.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{&lt;k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{&lt;k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(q)</annotation></semantics></math> and the tail process after <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q_{k}^{*}\;:=\;1+\sum_{t=1}^{h-k}T_{k+1:k+t},\qquad\Sigma_{k}\;:=\;1+\sum_{t=1}^{h-k}(2t+1)\,T_{k+1:k+t},\qquad V_{k}\;:=\;\Sigma_{k}\;-\;(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{*}\;:=\;1+\sum_{t=1}^{h-k}T_{k+1:k+t},\qquad\Sigma_{k}\;:=\;1+\sum_{t=1}^{h-k}(2t+1)\,T_{k+1:k+t},\qquad V_{k}\;:=\;\Sigma_{k}\;-\;(Q_{k}^{*})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so that, given <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1,C_{k}=1]=Q_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1,C_{k}=1]=Q_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Var}(G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1,C_{k}=1)=V_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Var}(G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1,C_{k}=1)=V_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="A2.SS5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unconditional</em> mean return-to-go at step <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}\;:=\;\mathbb{E}[G_{k}]\;=\;\sum_{t=k}^{h}s_{t}\;=\;s\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></munderover><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}\;:=\;\mathbb{E}[G_{k}]\;=\;\sum_{t=k}^{h}s_{t}\;=\;s\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use the unbiased reward-to-go REINFORCE block with the constant baseline <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}\;=\;\big(G_{k}-b_{k}\big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y),\qquad\bar{g}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}g_{k}^{(i)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}\;=\;\big(G_{k}-b_{k}\big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y),\qquad\bar{g}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}g_{k}^{(i)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since only step <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{&lt;k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{&lt;k}=1</annotation></semantics></math> is required for a contribution,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(C_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}{=}1)=\Big(\frac{C_{k}}{q}-\frac{1-C_{k}}{1-q}\Big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}=\frac{C_{k}-q}{q(1-q)}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)=\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(C_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}{=}1)=\Big(\frac{C_{k}}{q}-\frac{1-C_{k}}{1-q}\Big)\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}=\frac{C_{k}-q}{q(1-q)}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Mean.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(G_{k}-b_{k})\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]=\mathbb{E}[G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]-b_{k}=q\,Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(G_{k}-b_{k})\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]=\mathbb{E}[G_{k}\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]-b_{k}=q\,Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{k}-q\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{k}-q\mid C_{&lt;k}=1]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the cross term vanishes and</p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}=\mathbb{E}g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bar{g}_{k}=\mathbb{E}g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[\,G_{k}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\,\big]=s\,\frac{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}}{q(1-q)}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{k}(C_{k}-q)\,G_{k}\;\middle|\;C_{&lt;k}{=}1\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\big[\,G_{k}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y)\,\big]=s\,\frac{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}}{q(1-q)}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[C_{k}(C_{k}-q)\,G_{k}\;\middle|\;C_{&lt;k}{=}1\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s\,\frac{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}}{q(1-q)}\,(1-q)\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}\;=\;s\,Q_{k}^{*}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s\,\frac{\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}}{q(1-q)}\,(1-q)\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}\;=\;s\,Q_{k}^{*}\,\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Second moment and variance.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Condition on reach (<math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{&lt;k}{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{&lt;k}{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>). Writing <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C:=C_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C:=C_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> for the tail variable so that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{k}=C\,Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{k}=C\,Y</annotation></semantics></math> on reach,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{k}\|^{2}=\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}}{q^{2}(1-q)^{2}}\,(C-q)^{2}\,(C\,Y-b_{k})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{k}\|^{2}=\frac{\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}}{q^{2}(1-q)^{2}}\,(C-q)^{2}\,(C\,Y-b_{k})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking expectation over <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[(Y-b_{k})^{2}\mid C{=}1\right]=V_{k}+(Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[(Y-b_{k})^{2}\mid C{=}1\right]=V_{k}+(Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the conditional second moment</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|g_{k}\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,C_{&lt;k}{=}1\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\!\left[\|g_{k}\|^{2}\,\bigm|\,C_{&lt;k}{=}1\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{b_{k}^{2}}{1-q}+\frac{V_{k}+(Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k})^{2}}{q}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\left[\frac{b_{k}^{2}}{1-q}+\frac{V_{k}+(Q_{k}^{*}-b_{k})^{2}}{q}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unconditioning multiplies by <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> (probability of reach), and substituting <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k}=s\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k}=s\,q\,Q_{k}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from equation <a href="#A2.E10" title="In B.5 Dense rewards ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|g_{k}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|g_{k}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\Bigg[\frac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\frac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\frac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)\Bigg]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\Bigg[\frac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\frac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\frac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Subtracting <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbb{E}g_{k}\|^{2}=s^{2}(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{E}g_{k}\|^{2}=s^{2}(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from equation <a href="#A2.E13" title="In Second moment and variance. ‣ B.5 Dense rewards ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> gives the unconditional variance of the single-trajectory block:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|g_{k}-\mathbb{E}g_{k}\|^{2}=s\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\Bigg[\frac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\frac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\frac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)\Bigg]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|g_{k}-\mathbb{E}g_{k}\|^{2}=s\,\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\Bigg[\frac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\frac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\frac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">For the batch average <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{g}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> this variance scales as <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Signal-to-noise ratio.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining equation <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Mean. ‣ B.5 Dense rewards ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and equation <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Second moment and variance. ‣ B.5 Dense rewards ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and accounting for the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/N</annotation></semantics></math> factor,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{\mathrm{dense}}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>dense</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{\mathrm{dense}}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}{\dfrac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\dfrac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\dfrac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}{\dfrac{V_{k}}{q}+(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}\!\left(\dfrac{1}{q}-3s+s^{2}q+\dfrac{s^{2}q^{2}}{1-q}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,q\,(1-q)}{\dfrac{\Sigma_{k}}{(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}(1-q)+sq(sq-3(1-q))}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,q\,(1-q)}{\dfrac{\Sigma_{k}}{(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}(1-q)+sq(sq-3(1-q))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This form is the same as that in the terminal rewards only case, except with the ratio <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q^{*}_{k})^{2}/\Sigma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q^{*}_{k})^{2}/\Sigma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> replacing <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Regular tails.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under our initialization assumption that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\in[\delta,1-\delta]</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta^{t}\leq T_{k+1:k+t}\leq(1-\delta)^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{t}\leq T_{k+1:k+t}\leq(1-\delta)^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1+\delta\;\leq\;Q_{k}^{*}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{\delta},\qquad 1+3\delta\;\leq\;\Sigma_{k}\;\leq\;1+\sum_{t\geq 1}(2t+1)(1-\delta)^{t}=1+\frac{(1-\delta)(2+\delta)}{\delta^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1+\delta\;\leq\;Q_{k}^{*}\;\leq\;\frac{1}{\delta},\qquad 1+3\delta\;\leq\;\Sigma_{k}\;\leq\;1+\sum_{t\geq 1}(2t+1)(1-\delta)^{t}=1+\frac{(1-\delta)(2+\delta)}{\delta^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{(1+\delta)^{2}}{\,1+\frac{(1-\delta)(2+\delta)}{\delta^{2}}\,}\;\leq\;\frac{(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}{\Sigma_{k}}\;\leq\;\frac{1/\delta^{2}}{\,1+3\delta\,}\;=\;\Theta(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{(1+\delta)^{2}}{\,1+\frac{(1-\delta)(2+\delta)}{\delta^{2}}\,}\;\leq\;\frac{(Q_{k}^{*})^{2}}{\Sigma_{k}}\;\leq\;\frac{1/\delta^{2}}{\,1+3\delta\,}\;=\;\Theta(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, before the tail has been trained, the SNR for <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> scales as</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{\mathrm{dense}}(\theta_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SNR</mi><mi>dense</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{SNR}_{\mathrm{dense}}(\theta_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,q\,(1-q)}{(1-q)+sq(sq-3(1-q))}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;=\;\frac{N\,s\,q\,(1-q)}{(1-q)+sq(sq-3(1-q))},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">the same as in the curriculum case.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We should see similar <em id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">frontier</em> behaviour as we see in the uniform mixture case, as the SNR scales with the success probability <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we say horizon <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is at the frontier if <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i-1}\geq c\quad\text{for some fixed }c\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for some fixed </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i-1}\geq c\quad\text{for some fixed }c\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. To make <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (so that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\geq c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\geq c</annotation></semantics></math>) we require</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right)\;=\;\Theta(H)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle N\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\frac{1}{\varepsilon}\right)\;=\;\Theta(H),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">while the noiseless improvement is</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,\mathrm{dense}}\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>dense</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{(0)}_{k,\mathrm{dense}}\;=\;\Theta\!\left(\|\nabla_{\theta_{k}}q_{k}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, we have the same scaling and sample complexity as in curriculum learning. The wall clock time may be slightly lower as we do not prevent training at longer lengths <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq i</annotation></semantics></math> before <math id="A2.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i-1}\geq 1-\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i-1}\geq 1-\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Decreasing Sample Complexity for Longer Training Data</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Designing a cost-efficient curriculum ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we train with the sample distributions mentioned in Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix C Decreasing Sample Complexity for Longer Training Data ‣ h1: Bootstrapping LLMs to Reason over Longer Horizons via Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> up to saturation. From the explicit-horizon accuracies on our test set, we can see that the performance obtained from a uniform distribution of <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-horizon data can be matched with a more cost efficient skewed distribution as long as more compute is spent. However, this is a small search space that primarily shows such a property could exist. Here, we provide a more rigorous set of experiments to support this finding.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:79pt;vertical-align:-37.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-79.8pt,15.9pt) scale(0.713456322971953,0.713456322971953) ;">
